# Verification discipline

PlayKiln shipped avoidable defects that were only found by *running* the code, not
by reading it. Each rule below exists because it was violated once. They are not
style preferences; they are the fix.

## Never claim a script works until it ran

- Writing a script is half the job. Run it on real input before reporting it done.
- "The code looks correct" is not evidence. `node scripts/verify.mjs` is evidence, and the inline
  fixture set each check carries is what makes its own claim falsifiable.
- If a script cannot be run, say so explicitly instead of implying it works.

## Recursive copies must filter

- Any `cpSync` / `Copy-Item -Recurse` over a project tree must exclude build
  outputs, IDE state, and machine-local files: `build/`, `.gradle/`, `.kotlin/`,
  `.idea/`, `.cxx/`, `dist/`, `captures/`, `*.apk`, `*.aab`, `*.jks`, `*.so`,
  `local.properties`, `keystore.properties`.
- Before writing the copy step, list the source directory. Never assume what is in
  a directory you have not listed.
- Reuse the shared predicate (`scripts/new-slot.mjs` → `isExcludedScaffoldPath`)
  instead of re-implementing the filter somewhere else.

## Text rewriting must never touch binary files

- Any search/replace pass over a tree must skip files containing NUL bytes.
- Match whole tokens; a rewrite that fires inside a binary silently corrupts it and
  is invisible until a build fails.

## One source of truth, imported — never restated

- A value used by two scripts lives in one module and is imported.
  Namespace/applicationId rules belong to `scripts/lib/namespaces.mjs`.
- Never hand-write an error message that repeats a rule. Build the message from the
  check itself (`${pattern}`), so the wording cannot drift away from the logic.
  A hardcoded message telling users to pass `com.playkiln.*` while the regex
  required `com.gexetr.*` is exactly the defect this prevents.

## After changing a shared constant, sweep the repo

- A rename is not done until a repo-wide search finds zero leftovers.
- Search **all** textual forms, because the same prefix hides in several:
  plain (`com.x.y`), regex-escaped (`com\.x\.y`), string-escaped (`com\\.x\\.y`),
  and path form (`com/x/y`).
- Rename package *directories* too, not just file contents.
- Then prove it with the selftest's "no leftover reference" checks.

## Kotlin / Compose specifics that already broke once

- Compose-only apps do **not** bundle Material Components View libraries. A theme
  must not use `Theme.Material3.*` or `Theme.MaterialComponents.*` parents; use an
  `android:Theme.Material.*` parent or a Compose `MaterialTheme`.
- A `when` over a sealed type is exhaustive. Never add `else -> error(...)`; it
  removes the compiler's exhaustiveness check and hides new cases.

## Every repeated defect earns a regression check

- When a defect is fixed, add a check to the inline fixture set of the module that owns the rule
  (`scripts/core/*.mjs`, run by `node scripts/verify.mjs`) that fails on the old behaviour, then
  confirm the check fails when you reintroduce the defect.
- A check that cannot fail is not a check. Verify the sensor before trusting it.
- Record what happened in `harness/lessons.md` (symptom → root cause → fix class).
